---
layout: layouts/base.njk
permalink: /resume/
title: Résumé — Sarthak Bichhawa
desc: "The résumé, rendered from the same source of truth the site argues from — printable directly, with three PDF cuts attached."
ogImage: /og/resume.png
ogImageAlt: "Résumé — Sarthak Bichhawa, Sr. Data & Applied Scientist"
---
<section class="section-pad page-head resume-page">
  <div class="wrap">
    <nav class="crumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">‹ <a href="/">The brief</a></nav>

    <div class="reveal">
      <div class="sec-mark">The résumé — rev {{ facts.meta.resume_rev }}</div>
      <h1 class="sec-title">One record, <em>three cuts.</em></h1>
      <p class="sec-sub">
        This page renders from the same <a href="/colophon/">source of truth</a> as the
        rest of the site, so the résumé and the brief cannot contradict each other.
        Print it directly, or take the PDF cut that matches your screen.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="resume-actions reveal">
      {%- for r in facts.resumes %}
      <a href="{{ r.file }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn {{ 'btn-primary' if loop.first else 'btn-ghost' }}" data-goatcounter-click="resume-page-pdf-{{ loop.index }}">↓ {{ r.label }}</a>
      {%- endfor %}
      <button class="btn btn-mono" type="button" onclick="window.print()">⎙ print this page</button>
    </div>

    {% include "partials/resume-doc.njk" %}

    <p class="mono-note strip-note" style="margin-top:1.4rem;">
      // the tailored PDFs are printed from this page's variants at build time — <span class="g">they can't drift from the record.</span>
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
